   "title": "Healing, second pass: make the window one picture",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## What this graph does\n\nThe first pass (MiniMax H3 from a storyboard sheet, with the film's own drumming kept) gives a healed window whose frames do not yet share one grain and one surface. This pass runs the window through **Wan 2.1 VACE 14B** at a **low denoise (0.3)**: the model re-draws each frame only lightly, enough to unify grain, texture and the last traces of damage, not enough to change what is in it.\n\n**Input.** `window.mp4`: one 81-frame window of the first-pass result at 768 \u00d7 560. **Output.** `second_pass_*.png`, the refined frames, which the seam blend (`tools/seam_blend.py`) joins with the neighbouring windows."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    299
   ],
   "size": [
    560,
    259
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 14,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "What should and should not happen",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Should.** The same people, hands, drum and beater in the same places, the same movement, a single even grain across the frame, natural colour without the magenta of the faded reversal.\n\n**Should not.** Changed faces, extra or deformed fingers, a shorter or straighter beater, a violet or magenta cast, waxy skin, over-sharpening, text, invented objects. The negative prompt lists exactly these; if one appears, the window is rejected and the denoise lowered, never raised.\n\n**Settings that matter.** Denoise 0.3 is the whole point of the pass; 0.5 starts to redraw the drumming. Seed 0, 30 steps, CFG 4.5, euler / simple, shift 8."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    598
   ],
   "size": [
